  "body": {
    "id": "lem:unit-radius-admissible",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "In the nested Gaussian experiment, every \\(r>0\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal R_+\\). More precisely, if \\(e=(\\mathbf 1_T,0)\\), then every canonical maximizer exhausts the constraint \\(\\|Kh_r\\|_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}^{-1}}=r\\), and\n\\[\n\\omega'_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(r)\\ge\n\\|Ke\\|_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}^{-1}}^{-1}>0,\n\\qquad\n0<s_r=\\omega'_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(r)\n\\le\\frac{\\omega_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(r)-\\omega_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(0)}{r}\n\\le\\frac{\\omega_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(r)}r.\n\\]\nIn particular, \\(1\\in\\mathcal R_+\\), \\(0<s_1\\le\\omega_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(1)\\), and \\(0\\le b_1\\le\\omega_{\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{nest}}}(1)/2\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Rplus",
      "hmod",
      "K",
      "Sigma_nest",
      "omega",
      "omegaprime",
      "sddelta",
      "biasdelta",
      "T"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:index-range",
      "ass:terminal-range",
